$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the reaction of
azetidines with chloroformates. A solution of azetidine (1 mmol) in
dichloromethane (4 mL) was treated with chloroformate (1.5 eq.) and
stirred at rt overnight. The crude reaction mixture was next concentrated
under reduced pressure and purified by flash column chromatography on
silica gel. When the reaction was too slugish in dichloromethane
(compounds 13n-13r'), the reaction was run in refluxing acetonitrile.
(1R,2R,3S)-Methyl N -benzyl-(3-chloro-3-cyano-2-phenylpropyl)-carbamate
(13b). Starting from azetidine 12b.S2 Yield: 81 %; white solid; Mp: 71
°C; [α]D 20: +4 (c 1.6, CHCl3); 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6, 308K): δ
7.24-7.36 (m, 8H), 7.14 (d, J = 6.7 Hz, 2H), 5.66 (br. d, J = 6.4 Hz,
1H), 4.37 (A of AB syst., J = 12.6 Hz, 1H), 4.04 (B of AB syst., J = 12.6
Hz, 1H), 3.65-3.92 (br. m, 1H), 3.52-3.68 (br. m, 5H); 13C NMR (75 MHz,
DMSO-d6, 296K): δ 156.1, 137.3 and 136.6 (rotamers), 128.7, 128.5, 128.3,
128.0, 127.3, 127.0, 116.7, 54.9, 53.2 and 52.4 (rotamers), 49.4, 48.2
and 47.8 (rotamers), 45.0; ESIMS (positive mode): 366.0, 342,8, 284,9;
HRMS (CI, NH3) m/z calcd. for C19H20ClN2O2 [M+H]+ 343.1213, found
343.1198.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Reaction of azetidines with chloroformates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Vargas-Sanchez, Monica; Lakhdar, Sami; Couty, Francois; Evano, Gwilherm
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2006), 8(24), 5501-5504

