$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of N-Cbz protected amines 7a-d.
General Procedure. Hydrogen chloride (5.0 eq, 4M in 1,4-dioxane) was
added at room temperature over a solution of sulfinamine V (1.0 eq) in
MeOH (0.1M). After 30 minutes the deprotection was completed and the
solution was concentrated to dryness, the amine hydrochloride was taken
up in 1,4-dioxane (0.1M) and K2CO3 50 % water solution (2.0 eq) and
benzyl chloroformate (2.5 eq) were added consecutively. The solution was
stirred for 30 minutes at room temperature and concentrated under vacuum.
The mixture was poured into a separatory funnel over water and extracted
with dichloromethane. The combined organic extracts were washed with
brine, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, concentrated under vacuum and
purified by means of flash chromatography on silica gel using
hexane:diisopropyl ether 6:1 as eluent.
(1R)-N-Benzyloxycarbonyl-1-isopropyl-4-pentenamine (7a)
(1R)-N-Benzyloxycarbonyl-1-(4-methoxyphenyl)-4-pentenamine (7c) Amine 7c
was synthesized following the general procedure described above starting
from 110 mg of sulfinamine Vc (0.373 mmol) to afford 98 mg of a white
solid (81% yield). M.p.: 100- 101 ºC. [α]25 D= +17.2 (c 1.0, CHCl3). 1H
NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.82-1.92 (2H, m), 2.00-2.04 (2H, m), 3.80 (3H,
s), 4.65 (1H, m), 4.97-5.14 (5H, m), 5.80 (1H, ddt, J1 = 13.1 Hz, J2 =
10.5 Hz, J3 = 6.4 Hz), 6.87 (2H, d, J= 8.5 Hz), 7.20 (2H, d, J= 8.5 Hz),
7.34 (5H, m). 13C NMR (75.5 MHz, CDCl3) δ 30.3, 35.6, 54.4, 55.2, 66.6,
113.9, 115.2, 117.5, 128.0 (2C), 128.4, 134.3, 136.4, 137.5, 155.6,
158.8. HRMS (EI) calc. for C20H23NO3 [M+]: 325.1678. Found: 325.1673.
