$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
4-(2-Aminoethyl)-N-(9-fluorenylmethoxycarbonyl)phenylamine Hydrochloride
(1b); Typical Procedure To a soln of 4-aminophenethylamine (0.3 g, 2.3
mmol) in 10% aq AcOH (20 mL) was added FmocCl (0.6 g, 2.4 mmol) dissolved
in 1,4-dioxane (20 mL). After overnight stirring at r.t., Et2O (2 × 30
mL) was added to the reaction mixture to extract the nonpolar impurities.
The reaction mixture was then acidified with 2 N HCl to pH 1. The
precipitate was collected by filtration, washed with Et2O (15 mL) and
dried under reduced pressure overnight.
3-(Aminomethyl)-N-(9-fluorenylmethoxycarbonyl)phenylamine Hydrochloride
(Entry 4) White solid; yield: 80%. Mp 223-225 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CD3OD): δ = 7.83 (d, J = 7.4 Hz, 2 H), 7.71 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 2 H), 7.68
(m, 1 H), 7.32-7.44 (m, 6 H), 7.12-7.14 (m, 1 H), 4.53 (d, J = 6.5 Hz, 2
H), 4.30 (t, J = 6.5 Hz, 1 H), 4.08 (s, 2 H). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CD3OD): δ
= 154.58, 144.03, 141.49, 139.89, 133.97, 129.58, 127.69, 127.02, 124.97,
124.88, 123.10, 119.89, 119.78, 119.37, 66.55, 43.23. MS (ESI): m/z = 345
[M + H+].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A method for the selective protection of aromatic amines in the presence
of aliphatic amines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
