$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
4-(2-Aminoethyl)-N-(9-fluorenylmethoxycarbonyl)phenylamine Hydrochloride
(1b); Typical Procedure To a soln of 4-aminophenethylamine (0.3 g, 2.3
mmol) in 10% aq AcOH (20 mL) was added FmocCl (0.6 g, 2.4 mmol) dissolved
in 1,4-dioxane (20 mL). After overnight stirring at r.t., Et2O (2 × 30
mL) was added to the reaction mixture to extract the nonpolar impurities.
The reaction mixture was then acidified with 2 N HCl to pH 1. The
precipitate was collected by filtration, washed with Et2O (15 mL) and
dried under reduced pressure overnight. Protection with Fmoc (Table 1,
Second Yield Column)
3-(2-Aminoethyl)-N-(9-fluorenylmethoxycarbonyl)phenylamine Hydrochloride
(Entry 2) White solid; yield: 80%. Mp 183-184 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CD3OD): δ = 7.79 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 2 H), 7.68 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 2 H), 7.44
(br s, 1 H), 7.22-7.40 (m, 6 H), 6.95 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 1 H), 4.46 (d, J =
6.8 Hz, 2 H), 4.24 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 1 H), 3.15 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 2 H), 2.92
(t, J = 8.0 Hz, 2 H). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CD3OD): δ = 154.69, 144.05,
141.47, 139.54, 137.48, 129.31, 127.67, 127.02, 124.96, 123.29, 119.83,
119.07, 117.73, 66.55, 48.48, 40.70, 33.44. MS (ESI): m/z = 359 [M + H+].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A method for the selective protection of aromatic amines in the presence
of aliphatic amines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
