$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Unsymmetrical Ureas 6 A solution of compound 3 (0.7 mmol), THF (30 mL),
and amine 4 (0.7 mmol) was stirred at r.t. until compound 3 disappeared
(TLC monitoring). After adding another amine 4 (0.7 mmol) and DMAP (1.4
mmol) for unsymmetrical diaryl urea 6k and 6l, the mixture was refluxed
until carbamate 5 disappeared. After evaporation of the solvent, the
product was isolated by silica gel column chromatography (2.5 × 7-11 cm,
elution solvent: EtOAc-n-hexane = 1:2, v/v).
1,1-Diisopropyl-3-p-tolylurea (6i), yield 80%. mp 135 °C (lit.12 145 -
146 °C). Rf = 0.45 (EtOAc / n-hexane = 1:2, v/v). IR (KBr): 3328, 3034,
2999, 2970, 2931, 2869, 1633, 1595, 1527, 1515, 1428, 1332, 1240, 1055,
818, 609 cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 1.23 (d, 12H, J = 6.7 Hz),
2.21 (s, 3H), 3.76-3.85 (m, 2H), 7.00 (d, 2H, J = 8.3 Hz), 7.30 (d, 2H, J
= 8.4 Hz), 7.83 (bs, NH, D2O exchangeable). 13C NMR (75 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ
20.76, 21.67, 45.90, 120.60, 128.92, 130.43, 138.76, 154.42 Elemental
analysis calcd. for C14H22N2O: C, 71.76; H, 9.46; N, 11.95. Found: C,
71.78; H, 9.48; N, 11.98.
