$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
aromatic Alloc-, CBz-, Troc-carbamates To a solution of sodium azide
(0.110 g, 1.70 mmol), sodium tert-butoxide (14.4 mg, 0.150 mmol), and
carboxylic acid (1.00 mmol) in DME (10.0 mL) at 25 °C, was added the
chloroformate reagent (1.10mmol) (Allylchloroformate: 120 μL,
benzylchloroformate: 150 μL, or 2,2,2 trichloroethylchloroformate:112
μL). Then the resulting mixture was stirred at 75 °C (85 °C for Troc
derivatives). When the reaction is completed by GC analysis, the mixture
was diluted with dichloromethane and a preabsorptionon silica was made.
The crude carbamate was then purified by flash chromatography onsilica
gel. Benzyl benzofuran-2-ylcarbamate (30). The title compound was
prepared from 2-benzofuranbenzoicacid (162 mg, 1.00 mmol) according to
the general procedure. The desired carbamate 30 (214 mg, 80%) was
obtained as a yellow solid, after flash chromatography (20%
EtOAc/hexanes). Rf 0.41 (20%EtOAc/hexanes); mp 81 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.47-7.32 (m, 7H), 7.28 (s (br), 1H), 7.23-7.15 (m, 2H), 6.55 (s
(br), 1H), 5.27 (s, 2H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 151.8, 150.1, 147.6,
135.3,129.4, 128.65, 128.57, 128.4, 123.2, 122.5, 120.1, 110.2, 88.9,
67.9; IR 3287, 3149, 3063, 2962, 1703,1608, 1542, 1454, 1215, 1058, 733
cm-1; HMRS (ESI) calcd for C16H14NO3 [M+H]+: 268.0979. Found: 268.0968.
