$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the reaction of
azetidines with chloroformates. A solution of azetidine (1 mmol) in
dichloromethane (4 mL) was treated with chloroformate (1.5 eq.) and
stirred at rt overnight. The crude reaction mixture was next concentrated
under reduced pressure and purified by flash column chromatography on
silica gel. When the reaction was too slugish in dichloromethane
(compounds 13n-13r'), the reaction was run in refluxing acetonitrile.
[2S,4(1S)]-tert-Butyl
2-chloro-4-[methoxycarbonyl-(1-phenylethyl)-amino]-butanoate (13h).
Starting from azetidine 12h.S6 Yield: 78 %; colorless oil; [α] 20D: +21
(c 1.5, CHCl3); 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6, 353K): δ 7.27-7.40 (m, 5H),
5.29 (q, J = 7.1 Hz, 1H), 4.26-4.34 (m, 1H), 3.85 and 3.75 (dd, J = 5.3,
7.4 Hz , dd, J = 6.4, 7.4 Hz, rotamers, 1H), 3.66 and 3.62 (s, s,
rotamers, 3H), 3.03-3.26 (m, 2H), 1.85-2.01 (m, 1H), 1.57 and 1.53 (d, J
= 7.1, d, J = 7.2, rotamers, 3H), 1.42 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3,
294K): δ 169.8, 156.9, 140.8, 128.6, 128.5, 127.6, 127.3, 82.7 and 81.3
(rotamers), 56.8 and 56.3 (rotamers), 55.4 and 53.9 (rotamers), 52.7,
43.9, 34.6, 27.9, 17.3; ESIMS (positive mode): 377.7, 298.3; HRMS (CI,
NH3) m/z calcd. for C18H26ClNO4 [M+H]+ 355.1550, found 355.1571.
