$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: N-Benzyloxycarbonyl-4-pentenamine (2a) To a
suspension of LiAlH4 (1.13 g, 29.8 mmol) in Et2O (30 mL) at room
temperature, 4-pentenenitrile (0.99 mL, 9.94 mmol) was added dropwise.
After heating under reflux for two hours (monitored by TLC) the mixture
was allowed to reach room temperature. Then, Na2SO4·10H2O was added to
the mixture with vigorous stirring until grey LiAlH4 salts turned into
white. The suspension was filtered off through a sort pad of Celite® and
concentrated under vacuum. N-Benzyloxycarbonyl-2,2-difluoro-4-pentenamine
(2c) Compound 2c was synthesized following the procedure described above,
starting from 285 mg of 2,2-difluoro-4-pentenenitrile1 (2.43 mmol) to
afford 484 mg of 2c as a white solid in 78% yield (2 steps). M. p.:
28-30ºC. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.64 (2H, td, J HF = 16.2 Hz, J HH =
7.1 Hz), 3.59 (2H, td, J HF = 13.8 Hz, J HH = 6.5 Hz), 5.02 (1H, bs),
5.13 (2H, s), 5.20-5.26 (2H, m), 5.74- 5.88 (2H, m), 7.36 (5H, m). 19F
NMR (282.4 MHz, CDCl3) δ -104.39 (2F, q, JFH = 16.9 Hz). 13C NMR (75.5
MHz, CDCl3) δ 38.9 (t, 2JCF = 22.6 Hz), 44.8 (t, 2JCF = 30.2 Hz), 67.1,
120.8, 121.6 (t, 1 JCF = 241.6 Hz), 128.0, 128.1, 128.3, 128.4, 136.0,
156.3. HRMS (EI) calc. for C14H17F2NO2 [M+]: 255.1071. Found: 255.1030.
