$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM b) Preparation of the Mosher derivative (1R, 2’R)-12: To a solution of
the so-obtained residue from the removal of the allyloxycarbonyl group
reaction (where the isoindoline (R)-6 was present in a maximal amount of
0.0843 mmol) in dry CH2Cl2(0.9 mL), the (S)-Mosher’s acid chloride (20
μL, 0.105 mmol, 1.25 equiv.) and Et3N (15 μL, 0.105 mmol, 1.25 equiv.)
were added, under inert atmosphere. The mixture was stirred overnight at
room temperature and then CH2Cl2(10 mL) was added. The organic layer was
washed with H2O (2 x 10 mL), dried with Na2SO4 and concentrated in vacuo.
The resulting residue was purified by column chromatography (8%
EtOAc/hexane). The corresponding Mosher derivative (1R, 2’R)-12 with 22%
de (25 mg, 76% isolated yield) b) Preparation of the Mosher derivative
(1R, 2’R)-12: It was obtained as was described in the previous section
when using the allyl carbamate as starting material was the. In this case
the corresponding Mosher derivative (1R, 2’R)-12 was obtained with a
significant loss of enantiopurity during the steps a) and b)
(deprotection and formation of Mosher derivatives), although less than in
the case of the Alloc derivative (R)-10 as starting material (22% de),
reaching a 67% de as is shown in the figure S1 below. (18 mg, 78%
isolated yield).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, alternative preparation shown lower yield (using
different protecting group)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
