$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Synthesis of Compounds 34-45. A solution of the
appropiate amine (1.62 mmol) was added to a solution of
10H-phenoxazine-10-carbonyl chloride (25, 200 mg, 0.81 mmol) in DCE (2
mL) at 0 °C under an argon atmosphere. The suspension was allowed to warm
to room temperature and stirred for 2 h. Then the reaction was quenched
with water (30 mL), and the aqueous portion was extracted with DCM (3 ×
20 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with brine (50 mL), dried
with MgSO4, and evaporated. Pure compounds were isolated after
crystallization (for crystallization solvents see the individual
compounds). N-Methyl-10H-phenoxazine-10-carboxamide (34). Synthesized
according to general procedure with methyl amine (0.81 mL, 2M in THF,
1.62 mmol). After crystallization (hexane:ethyl acetate 3:1) the product
was obtained as colorless needles (151 mg, 78 % yield). 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.52 (dd, J = 7.5, 1.5 Hz, 2H), 7.16-7.06 (m, 6H), 5.33 (br s,
1H, NH), 2.85 (d, J = 4.5 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 155.3,
151.2, 129.5, 126.3, 124.5, 123.7, 117.0, 27.5. LC-MS (m/z): positive
mode 241 [M+H]+, 481 [2M+H]+; Purity by HPLC-UV (254 nm)-ESI-MS: 100.0 %;
mp 150-151 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Substituted Phenoxazine and Acridone Derivatives: Structure-Activity
Relationships of Potent P2X4 Receptor Antagonists
