$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Reduction
Nitroarenes to N,O-Bisprotected N-Aryl Hydroxylamines To a solution of
nitroarene (10 mmol) in THF-H2O (60 mL, 2:1) was added NH4Cl (11 mmol),
and the mixture was cooled to 0 °C. The chloroformate (30 mmol) was added
via syringe, and after 5 min Zn powder (40 mmol) was added in one
portion. After 2 h the phases were separated and the organic layer
diluted with Et2O (60 mL), washed with sat. NaHCO3 (2 × 50 mL), H2O (50
mL), and brine (50 mL). The organic layer was dried over MgSO4 and the
solvent removed under reduced pressure. Purification by column
chromatography on SiO2 (EtOAc-PE, 1:5 to 1:3) gave the bisprotected
hydroxylamine 5 (34-81%). Methyl N-4-Tolyl-N-(methoxycarbonyloxy)
Carbamate, yield 78%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.34 (d, 2 H, J= 8.1
Hz), 7.19 (d, 2 H, J= 8.1 Hz), 3.90 (s, 3 H), 3.83 (s, 3 H), 2.36 (s, 3
H). 13C NMR (62.5 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 154.8, 154.3, 138.4, 136.8, 129.7,
125.1, 56.3, 53.9, 21.1. HRMS: m/z calcd for [M + H]+ C11H11NO5:
240.0866; found: 240.0868.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Facile procedure for the synthesis of N-aryl-N-hydroxy carbamates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Porzelle, Achim; Woodrow, Michael D.; Tomkinson, Nicholas C. O.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2009), (5), 798-802

