$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
aromatic Alloc-, CBz-, Troc-carbamates To a solution of sodium azide
(0.110 g, 1.70 mmol), sodium tert-butoxide (14.4 mg, 0.150 mmol), and
carboxylic acid (1.00 mmol) in DME (10.0 mL) at 25 °C, was added the
chloroformate reagent (1.10mmol) (Allylchloroformate: 120 μL,
benzylchloroformate: 150 μL, or 2,2,2 trichloroethylchloroformate:112
μL). Then the resulting mixture was stirred at 75 °C (85 °C for Troc
derivatives). When the reaction is completed by GC analysis, the mixture
was diluted with dichloromethane and a preabsorptionon silica was made.
The crude carbamate was then purified by flash chromatography onsilica
gel. Allyl naphthalen-3-ylcarbamate (8). The title compound was prepared
from 2-naphtanoic acid (172mg, 1.00 mmol) according to the general
procedure. The desired carbamate 8 (175 mg, 77%) was obtained as a pale
brown solid after flash chromatography (20% EtOAc/hexanes). Rf 0.31
(20%EtOAc/hexanes); mp 98 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.90-7.88 (m,
3H), 7.69 (d, J = 8Hz, 1H),7.54-7.47 (m, 3H), 7.13 (s (br), 1H),
6.09-5.99 (m, 1H), 5.42 (d, J = 17 Hz, 1H), 5.31 (d, J = 10 Hz,1H), 4.76
(d, J = 6 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 154.1, 133.9, 132.4, 132.3,
128.6, 126.7,126.1, 125.9, 125.7, 125.0, 120.4, 119.1, 118.2, 66.0 ; IR
3265, 3050, 2940, 1693, 1525, 1501, 1253,1230, 1103, 990, 785, 764 cm-1;
HMRS (ESI) calcd for C14H14NO2 [M+H]+: 228.1024. Found: 228.1019.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
