$DATUM N-acetyl-N-ethoxycarbonyl-(1-ferrocenylethyl)amine (6) n-BuLi (1.6 M in
hexane, 1 mmol) was added to a cold (−25 °C) solution of bromo-amide 4
(0.5 mmol) in dry THF (5 ml) and stirred at −25 °C for 2 hours. After
that ClCOOEt (0.6 mmol) was added and mixture was stirred for an
additional hour at the same temperature, poured into the water, extracted
with CH2Cl2, washed with saturated aqueous solution of NaCl, dried, and
evaporated. TLC-purification of crude product with CH2Cl2/ diethyl ether
(15 : 1). yellow product 6, yield: 154 mg (77%) IR (CH2Cl2) νmax/cm−1:
1734 (C=O, COOEt), 1693 (C=O, COCH3). 1H-NMR (CDCl3) δ/ppm: 5.9 (q, 1H,
CH), 4.05–4.3 (m, 11H, 9HFc + CH2), 2.41 (s, 3H,COCH3), 1.64 (s, 3H,
CHCH3), 1.18 (t, 3H, CH2CH3, 3J = 7.2 Hz).13C-NMR, APT (CDCl3) δ/ppm:
172.28 (COCH3), 154.67 (COOEt), 88.43 (C-1, Fc), 70.41 (Cpunsubst), 69.96
(C-3, Fc), 69.29 (C-4, Fc), 69.0 (C-2, Fc), 67.53 (C-5, Fc), 62.34 (CH2),
49.26 (CHCH3), 29.54 (COCH3), 17.43 (CHCH3), 13.76 (CH2CH3). HR-MS: calc.
for C17H21NO3Fe = 343.08710, found: 343.08700. MS (EI): m/z = 343 (100)
[M]+, 301 (5) [M+ −Ac], 271 (5) [M+ −COOEt], 251 (17) [M+ −CpCHMe], 166
(69), 163 (41) [FeCpCHMeNH], 121 (35) [CpFe], 91 (20) [CpCHMe], 56 (10)
[Fe]. Crystallographic data: C17H21FeNO3, Formula (wt./g mol−1) 343.20,
Crystal dimensions/mm 0.2x0.15x0.1, Space group P21/n, a (Å) 14.1895(6),
b (Å) 7.9961(3), c (Å) 14.4287(5), α (°) 90, β (°) 96.163(3), γ (°) 90.
