$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Compounds 17-20. To a solution of lithium diisopropylamide (LDA, 1 mL, 2
M in tetrahydrofuran (THF), 2 mmol) was added a solution of phenoxazine
(187 mg, 1 mmol) and the corresponding carbamoyl chloride (2.5 mmol) in
dry THF (3 mL) at 0 °C under an argon atmosphere. The mixture was allowed
to warm to room temperature and stirred for 2 h. Then the reaction was
quenched with aqueous HCl (30 mL, 0.4 M), and the aqueous portion was
extracted with DCM (3 × 20 mL). The combined organic layers were washed
with brine (50 mL) and dried over MgSO4. Pure compounds were isolated
after flash chromatography (for conditions see the individual compounds)
and crystallized (for crystallization solvents see the individual
compounds). N,N-Diethyl-10H-phenoxazine-10-carboxamide (18). Synthesized
using diethylcarbamylchloride (320 DL, 2.5 mmol). After flash
chromatography (petroleum ether:ethyl acetate 9:1) and crystallization
(petroleum ether, -18 °C) the product was obtained as colorless needles
(216 mg, 77 % yield). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.84-6.77 (m, 6H),
6.66-6.64 (m, 2H), 3.49 (q, J = 7.5 Hz, 4H), 1.23 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 6H).
13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 154.4, 144.3, 130.3, 123.7, 122.8, 116.1,
114.0, 42.6, 13.7; LC-MS (m/z): positive mode 283 [M+H]+; Purity by
HPLC-UV (254 nm)-ESI-MS: 100.0 %; mp 74-75 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Substituted Phenoxazine and Acridone Derivatives: Structure-Activity
Relationships of Potent P2X4 Receptor Antagonists
