$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4. General procedure for the synthesis of ethoxy carbonyl derivatives.4b
To a solution of prepared crude amine in anhydrous CH2Cl2 was added DMAP
(25 mg, 10%), Et3N (0.30 ml, 1.1 mmol, 1.1 eq.) and ethyl chloroformate
(0.2 ml, 1.1 mmol, 1.1 eq.). The resulting mixture was stirred for 3 h.
It was then quenched with water and extracted with CH2Cl2 (3×30 mL). The
organic phase was collected and dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. Solvent was
evaporated under vacuum and the residue was purified by chromatography
with PE/EA (6/1) giving the corresponding product. It was then used for
GC analysis on the chiral column. (S)-(1-Phenyl-ethyl)-carbamic acid
ethyl ester (ethoxycarbonyl derivative of 3):4bPurified by column
chromatography on silica gel/hexane: ethylacetate (6/1) as a white solid;
yield 77% (0.150g) 1H NMR (400MHz): δ 1.2 (m, 3H), 1.5 (d, 3H), 4.1 (m,
2H), 4.85 (m, 1H), 7.2-7.5 (m, 5H).
