$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
11-Bromo-1,3-dimethyl-3,3a,6,7,12,12b,13,13a-octahydroindolo[2,3-a]isoxazolo[4,3-g]quinolizin-4(1H)-one
(16). tert-Butyldimethyl(vinyloxy)silane (10) (8.42 g, 124 mmol) and
trans-crotonyl chloride (8.42 g, 81 mmol) were added to a solution of
β-dihydrocarboline 8 (15.3 g, 62 mmol) in THF (250 mL) at -78 °C, and the
reaction was stirred for 10 min. The bath was removed and the reaction
stirred at room temperature for 75 min, whereupon saturated aqueous
NaHCO3 (300 mL) and EtOAc (300 mL) were added. The layers were separated,
and the aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc (2 × 300 mL). The combined
organic layers were washed with H2O (300 mL) and brine (300 mL), dried
(Na2SO4), filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure. 14.4 g of
crude material that was dissolved in anhydrous toluene (200 mL).
N-Methylhydroxylamine hydrochloride (3.99 g, 48 mmol) and Et3N (6.1 g,
8.4 mL, 60 mmol) were added, and the mixture was heated under reflux with
continuous removal of H2O using a Dean-Stark trap for 3 h. The reaction
mixture was cooled to room temperature and partitioned between saturated
aqueous NaHCO3 (200 mL) and EtOAc (400 mL). The layers were separated,
and the aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc (2 × 200 mL). The combined
organic layers were washed with H2O (200 mL) and brine (200 mL), dried
(Na2SO4), and concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude residue was
purified by flash column chromatography eluting with EtOAc. 8.95 g of 16
(37% over two steps) as a tan solid; LCMS purity: 95%. Representative
Procedure for N-O Bond Cleavage:
1-(Hydroxyethyl)-2-(methylamino)-1,2,3,6,7,12b-hexahydroindolo[2,3-a]quinolizin-4(12H)-one
(18). Sodium borohydride (0.73 g, 19.3 mmol) was added slowly over 5 min
to a solution of isoxazolidine 14 (1.00 g, 3.21 mmol) and NiCl2·6H2O
(1.53 g, 2.0 mmol) in MeOH (60 mL). The reaction mixture was stirred for
2 h, and the solvent was removed under reduced pressure. The residue was
dissolved in CH2Cl2 (30 mL), and 30% aqueous NH4OH (30 mL) was added. The
mixture was stirred for 1.5 h, and the layers were separated. The aqueous
layer was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 × 20 mL), and the combined organic
layers were washed with brine (50 mL), dried (Na2SO4), and concentrated
under reduced pressure. The crude residue was purified by flash column
chromatography on Florisil® eluting with EtOAc/MeOH (10 : 1). 680 mg
(68%) of 18 as a yellow oil; LCMS purity: 96%.
3-(1-Hydroxyethyl)-2-(methylamino)-8-phenyl-1,2,3,6,7,12b-hexahydroindolo[2,3-a]quinolizin-4(12H)-one
(25{1}). Prepared according to the representative procedure for N-O bond
cleavage. Purification: recrystallized from MeOH.
8-(3-Fluorophenyl)-3-(1-hydroxyethyl)-2-(methylamino)-1,2,3,6,7,12b-hexa-hydroindolo[2,3-a]quinolizin-4(12H)-one
(25{5}). Prepared according to the representative procedure for N-O bond
cleavage. Purification: recrystallized from MeOH/Et2O. Yield: 77% (240 mg
colorless powder); LCMS purity: 98%. Data: mp 229-230 °C; 1H NMR (400
MHz) δ 7.14-7.08 (comp, 2 H), 6.95-6.89 (comp, 2 H), 6.87-6.83 (m, 1 H),
6.81-6.76 (m, 1 H), 6.69 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1 H), 4.61-4.55 (m, 1 H), 4.48
(dd, J = 12.8, 4.0 Hz, 1 H), 3.94 (dq, J = 12.0, 6.0 Hz, 1 H), 3.04 (dd,
J = 4.0, 4.0 Hz, 1 H), 2.48-2.35 (comp, 3 H), 2.29-2.21 (m, 1 H), 2.21
(s, 3 H), 1.95 (ddd, J = 11.2, 10.8, 10.8 Hz, 1 H), 1.80 (d, J = 15.6 Hz,
1 H), 0.99 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 3 H); 13C NMR (100 MHz) δ 168.9, 162.0 (J =
244 Hz), 143.4,136.7, 133.4, 128.8, 125.1, 123.9, 121.3, 120.4, 116.0,
113.3, 110.5, 107.6, 67.2, 55.6, 52.9, 49.4, 40.7, 33.4, 29.9, 23.6,
21.9; IR (neat) 3252, 2932, 1624, 1439, 1290, 785 cm-1; mass spectrum
(ESI) m/z 408.2085 [C24H27N3O2F (M+1) requires 408.2082].
