$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of
Compounds 12-14. Benzoyl chloride (163 μL, 1.4 mmol) was added to a
solution of phenoxazine (187 mg, 1.0 mmol) and triethylamine (209 μL, 1.5
mmol) in dichloroethane (DCE, 3 mL) at 0 °C under argon. The resulting
mixture was stirred at room temperature for 2 h. Then the reaction was
quenched with aqueous HCl solution (20 mL, 0.5 M), and the aqueous
portion was extracted with dichloromethane (DCM) (3 × 20 mL). The organic
layers were combined, dried over MgSO4, and subsequently evaporated. Pure
compounds were isolated after flash chromatography (for conditions see
the individual compounds) and crystallized (for crystallization solvents
see the individual compounds).
(4-Chlorophenyl)(10H-phenoxazin-10-yl)methanone (14). Synthesized using
4-chlorobenzoyl chloride (180 DL, 1.4 mmol). The mixture was stirred at
80 °C for 6 h. After purification by flash chromatography (petroleum
ether:ethyl acetate 95:5) and crystallization (hexane:ethyl acetate 3:1)
the product was obtained as a yellow powder (248 mg, 77 % yield). 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.38-7.35 (m, 4H), 7.25 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H), 7.16-7.14
(m, 4H), 6.98-6.95 (m, 2H). 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.0, 150.3,
136.8, 133.4, 130.5, 129.9, 128.4, 126.7, 124.6, 123.4, 116.8. LC-MS
(m/z): positive mode 322 [M+H]+, 643 [2M+H]+; Purity by HPLC-UV (254
nm)-ESI-MS: 100.0 %; mp 136-137 °C.
