$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A. General procedure for preparation of substrate 1 (1d as representative
Example) To a round bottom flask equipped with magnetic stir bar,
L-tyrosine (200 mg, 1.2 mmol) was added and dissolved in DMF (8.0 mL,
0.15 M) followed by the addition of EtN3 (157 mg, 1.56 mmol, 1.3 eq.) and
DMAP (7.5 mg, 0.06 mmol, 0.05 eq.). The reaction flask was cooled in ice
water for 15 minutes and CbzCl (224 mg, 1.32 mmol, 1.1 eq.) was added
drop wise over 5 minutes. The reaction was monitored by TLC and until the
starting material was consumed over 5 hours. The mixture was diluted with
EtOAc (100 mL) and washed by HCl solution (1.0 M), saturated NaHCO3
(aq.), brine and then dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. The solvent was
removed under reduced pressure to give the crude residue. The amino
alcohol was then dissolved in dry THF (6.0 mL, 0.15 M) and methyl allyl
carbonate (157 mg, 1.35 mmol, 1.5 eq.) and the palladium catalyst (52 mg,
0.045 mmol, 0.05 eq.) were added. The solution was kept under argon
protection and heated to 60 °C for 5 hours. Once TLC indicated the
completion of the reaction, the mixture was diluted with EtOAc (100 mL).
The organic phase was washed by HCl solution (1.0 M), saturated NaHCO3
(aq.) and brine and then dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. The solvent was
removed under reduced pressure to provide the crude residue. Flash silica
gel chromatography (Ethyl Acetate/Hexane 10:90) was then applied to give
294 mg (92%) of the allyl ether intermediate. The allyl ether (294 mg,
0.83 mmol) was then dissolved in dichloromethane (4 mL, 0.2 M). MVK (290
mg, 4.15 mmol, 5.0 equiv.) was added in under argon protection.
Hoveyda-Grubbs II catalyst (10 mg, 0.016 mmol, 0.02 equiv.) was added in
the reaction mixture. The reaction mixture was then warmed up to 45 °C
and kept stirring for 4 hours, until the TLC indicated the completion of
reaction. The solvent was removed under reduced pressure to give a
residue. Flash silica gel chromatography (Ethyl Acetate/Hexane 25:75) was
then applied to give the intramolecular aza-Michael precursor 1d 554 mg,
yield 90%. (S,E)-benzyl
(2-((4-oxopent-2-en-1-yl)oxy)-2-phenylethyl)carbamate (4a). Purified by
flash chromatography (EtOAc/Hexane). Colorless oil (yield: 76% over 3
steps). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 7.38-7.29 (m, 10 H), 6.71 (dt, J =
16.0 Hz, J = 9.0 Hz, 1 H), 6.30 (d, J = 16.0 Hz, 1 H), 5.23 (bs, 1 H),
5.14-5.08 (m, 2 H), 4.47-4.45 (m, 1 H), 4.1-3.99 (m, 2 H), 3.59-3.54 (m,
1 H), 3.35-3.29 (m, 1 H), 2.24 (s, 3 H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
198.1, 156.2, 142.7, 138.5, 136.4, 130.1, 128.7, 128.5, 128.4, 128.1,
126.6, 81.1, 67.4, 66.7, 47.2, 27.1; HRMS calculated for [C21H23NO4+H]+:
354.1705, found: 354.1705.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective (stage 1), stereoselective (stage 3), intermediates after
each stage could be isolated, reactant assumed (chiral aminoalcohol),
metathesis reaction (stage 3), dropwise addition of Cbz-Cl (stage 1,
substage 1)
