$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: N-Cbz-, N-Moc-and N-Fmoc-Protected Proline
Derivatives 2f-i, 2k and 2l; General Procedure The solvent and the
reagents (including equivalents and the order of addition) are given in
Table 2. In general, a suspension of L-proline (1; 9-11 mmol, 1 equiv)
and Et3N (or DIPEA in the case of 2l) in CHCl3 ([1] = 0.3 mol/L) was
cooled to -20 °C and treated very slowly with a soln of PG-Cl (PG = Cbz,
Moc, Fmoc) in CHCl3 ([PG-Cl] = 2 mol/L). The cooling bath was removed and
the mixture was stirred at r.t. for 0.5-1 h; full conversion into 7b-d
was indicated by formation of a clear solution. Then, the reaction
mixture was cooled to 0 °C, treated with additional reagents (see Table
2, ‘Reagents’ column) and stirred at r.t. overnight. For workup, the
reaction mixture was either filtered with EtOAc-cyclohexane (1:1) through
a layer of silica gel or diluted with MTBE (and filtered, when DCC was
used), washed with 1 M HCl, sat. NaHCO3 soln and brine, dried over MgSO4
and concentrated under reduced pressure. All products were purified by
column chromatography on silica gel (EtOAc-cyclohexane; for 2l:
MeOH-EtOAc, 1:50). Methyl N-(Benzyloxycarbonyl)-L-prolinate (2f; Table 2,
Entry 1) N-Cbz-L-proline-Derived Weinreb Amide 2h [Benzyl
(S)-2-{[Methoxy(methyl)amino]carbonyl}pyrrolidine-1-carboxylate] Yield:
2.03 g (76%); pale yellow oil. [α]D20 -2.5 (c 2.445, CHCl3). IR (ATR):
3028, 2970, 2939, 2879, 1702, 1668, 1607, 1443, 1405, 1352, 1318, 1207,
1171, 1116, 1082 cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.32-7.27 (m, 5 H,
C6H5), 5.17-4.98 (m, 2 H, CH2Ph), 4.73/4.62 (2 × dd, J = 8.2, 3.4, 8.3,
3.7 Hz, 1 H, NCH), 3.76 (s, 3 H, OCH3, one rotamer), 3.68-3.57 (m, 1 H,
NCHH), 3.55-3.44 (m, 1 H, NCHH), 3.36 (s, 3 H, OCH3, second rotamer),
3.18 (s, 3 H, NCH3, one rotamer), 3.06 (s, 3 H, NCH3, second rotamer),
2.24-2.10 (m, 1 H, NCHCHH), 2.07-1.95 (m, 1 H, NCH2CHH), 1.94-1.78 (m, 2
H, NCHCHH, NCH2CHH). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 172.8 [CH(CO)],
154.9/154.2 [N(CO)], 136.7/136.6 (CH2CPh),
128.4/128.3/128.2/127.9/127.8/127.7 (5 × CHPh), 67.1/66.8 (CH2Ph),
61.3/60.8 (OCH3), 56.9/56.5 (NCH), 47.2/46.7 (NCH2), 32.1 (NCH3),
30.5/29.6 (NCHCH2), 24.2/23.4 (NCH2CH2). LRMS (EI): m/z (%) = 232 (5),
204 (25), 160 (25), 91 (100), 65 (10).
