$DATUM 4-Nitrophenyl methyl(n-pentyl)carbamate. A solution of
N-methyl-n-pentan-1-amine (200 mg, 1.98 mmol), Et3N (826 μl, 5.94 mmol),
and p-nitrophenyl chloroformate (399 mg, 1.98 mmol) in dry DMF (20 mL)
was stirred under an argon atmosphere at room temperature. After 2 h,
water (30 mL) was added and the mixture was extracted with Et2O (3 × 10
mL). The combined extracts were dried, concentrated under reduced
pressure, and the residue was purified by silica gel column
chromatography to afford 4-nitrophenyl methyl(n-pentyl)carbamate (375 mg,
76% yield). TLC: 20% EtOAc/hexanes, Rf ~ 0.72; 1H NMR (300 MHz) δ 8.24
(d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 7.28 (dd, J = 7.0, 1.8 Hz, 2H), 3.32-3.44 (m, 2H),
3.05 and 2.97 (s, 3H for two rotamers in 55/45 ratio), 1.61-1.70 (m, 2H),
1.24-1.42 (m, 4H), 0.92 (t, J = 6.6 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (75 MHz) δ 156.7,
153.6, 142.2, 125.2, 125.1, 122.4, 49.74, 35.0, 38.9, 27.8, 27.12, 22.59,
22.55, 14.18; HRMS calcd for C13H18N2O4 [M+1]+ 267.1345, found 267.1343.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 14,15-Epoxyeicosa-5,8,11-trienoic Acid (14,15-EET) Surrogates Containing
Epoxide Bioisosteres: Influence upon Vascular Relaxation and Soluble
Epoxide Hydrolase Inhibition
