$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure: An oven dried 50 mL flask
was charged with Me3Al (2.0M in Hexanes, 6.6 mmol, 3.3 mL) and dry
triethylamine (0.66 mmol, 92 μL) was added dropwise under argon. At room
temperature, alkyne (6.9 mmol) was added dropwise and the reaction
mixture was stirred at 60°C for 4 hours. The solution was allowed to cool
to room temperature and the corresponding nitrile (3 mmol) in dry toluene
(1 mL) was added dropwise. The reaction was stirred at 60°C for 16 hours
under argon, cooled to room temperature and cannulated dropwise to a
solution of chloroformate (15 mmol) in dry THF (5 mL) at -78°C. The
reaction mixture was warmed up to room temperature over 1h and stirred at
the same temperature for an extra hour. EtOAc (10 mL) was added followed
by DROPWISE addition of Rochelle salt (saturated aqueous solution, 20 mL)
under VIGOROUS STIRRING, and the cloudy light orange mixture was stirred
for 1 hour. At room temperature, the organic fraction was recovered,
rinsed with NaHCO3 (saturated aqueous solution, 30 mL), dried over MgSO4,
concentrated under vacuum and the crude material purified by column
chromatography (EtOAc/petroleum ether). (Z)-ethyl
(1-phenylhept-2-yn-1-ylidene)carbamate (11): 11 was prepared following
the general procedure and the reaction was performed with AlMe3 (2.0M in
hexanes, 19.8 mmol, 9.9 mL), triethylamine (1.9 mmol, 250 μL), 1-hexyne
(20 mmol, 2.2 mL), benzonitrile (9 mmol, 927 μL) and ethyl chloroformate
(27 mmol, 2.55 mL). Purification by flash chromatography (gradient 5-10%
EtOAc/petroleum ether). (Z)-allyl
(2,2-dimethylnon-4-yn-3-ylidene)carbamate (S9). S9 was prepared following
the general procedure and the reaction was performed with AlMe3 (2.0M in
hexanes, 10 mmol, 5 mL), triethylamine (0.9 mmol, 125 μL), 1-hexyne (10
mmol, 1.1 mL), trimethylacetonitrile (5 mmol, 554.2 μL) and allyl
chloroformate (25 mmol, 2.65 mL). Purification by flash chromatography
(gradient 0-5% EtOAc/petroleum ether). Colorless oil (75%, 933.8 mg).
Rf=0.35 (5% EtOAc/ hexanes); IR (neat) 2923, 2831, 2188, 1709, 1596,
1438, 1344, 1220, 1195, 1156 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ=6.02-5.94
(m, 1H), 5.41-5.35 (m, 1H), 5.28-5.24 (m, 1H), 4.71-4.68 (m, 2H), 2.38
(t, J=7.0 Hz, 2H), 1.57-1.40 (m, 4H), 1.21 (s, 9H), 0.92 (t, J=7.2 Hz,
3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ=166.7, 163.1, 132.1, 118.7, 102.2, 73.9,
67.1, 40.1, 29.9, 27.3, 21.8, 19.0, 13.5; HRMS (ESI) Calcd for
C15H23NNaO2 (M+Na)+: 272.1621; found 272.1626.
