$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A. General procedure for preparation of
substrate 1 (1d as representative Example) To a round bottom flask
equipped with magnetic stir bar, L-tyrosine (200 mg, 1.2 mmol) was added
and dissolved in DMF (8.0 mL, 0.15 M) followed by the addition of EtN3
(157 mg, 1.56 mmol, 1.3 eq.) and DMAP (7.5 mg, 0.06 mmol, 0.05 eq.). The
reaction flask was cooled in ice water for 15 minutes and CbzCl (224 mg,
1.32 mmol, 1.1 eq.) was added drop wise over 5 minutes. The reaction was
monitored by TLC and until the starting material was consumed over 5
hours. The mixture was diluted with EtOAc (100 mL) and washed by HCl
solution (1.0 M), saturated NaHCO3 (aq.), brine and then dried over
anhydrous Na2SO4. The solvent was removed under reduced pressure to give
the crude residue. The amino alcohol was then dissolved in dry THF (6.0
mL, 0.15 M) and methyl allyl carbonate (157 mg, 1.35 mmol, 1.5 eq.) and
the palladium catalyst (52 mg, 0.045 mmol, 0.05 eq.) were added. The
solution was kept under argon protection and heated to 60 °C for 5 hours.
Once TLC indicated the completion of the reaction, the mixture was
diluted with EtOAc (100 mL). The organic phase was washed by HCl solution
(1.0 M), saturated NaHCO3 (aq.) and brine and then dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4. The solvent was removed under reduced pressure to provide the
crude residue. Flash silica gel chromatography (Ethyl Acetate/Hexane
10:90) was then applied to give 294 mg (92%) of the allyl ether
intermediate. The allyl ether (294 mg, 0.83 mmol) was then dissolved in
dichloromethane (4 mL, 0.2 M). MVK (290 mg, 4.15 mmol, 5.0 equiv.) was
added in under argon protection. Hoveyda-Grubbs II catalyst (10 mg, 0.016
mmol, 0.02 equiv.) was added in the reaction mixture. The reaction
mixture was then warmed up to 45 °C and kept stirring for 4 hours, until
the TLC indicated the completion of reaction. The solvent was removed
under reduced pressure to give a residue. Flash silica gel chromatography
(Ethyl Acetate/Hexane 25:75) was then applied to give the intramolecular
aza-Michael precursor 1d 554 mg, yield 90%. (S,E)-benzyl
(2-((4-oxopent-2-en-1-yl)oxy)-2-phenylethyl)carbamate (4a). Purified by
flash chromatography (EtOAc/Hexane). (S,E)-benzyl
(1-cyclohexyl-3-((4-oxopent-2-en-1-yl)oxy)propan-2-yl)carbamate
(1f).Purified by flash chromatography (EtOAc/Hexane). Colorless oil
(yield: 75% over 3 steps). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 7.36-7.30 (m, 5
H), 6.75 (dt, J = 16.0 Hz, J = 8.5 Hz, 1 H), 6.27 (d, J = 16.0 Hz, 1 H),
5.11 (m, 2 H), 4.87 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.18-4.12 (m, 2 H), 3.92 (bs, 1
H), 3.50-3.44 (m, 2 H), 2.26 (s, 3 H), 1.82-1.78 (m, 1 H), 1.70-1.65 (m,
4 H), 1.42-1.38 (m, 2 H), 1.35-1.28 (m, 1 H), 1.25-1.12 (m, 3 H),
1.00-0.28 (m, 2 H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 198.0, 155.9, 142.8,
136.5, 130.1, 128.4, 128.0, 127.9, 73.3, 69.8, 66.5, 59.2, 48.3, 42.1,
39.6, 34.1, 33.7, 32.8, 27.2, 26.4, 26.2, 26.1; HRMS calculated for
[C22H31NO4+H]+: 374.2331, found: 374.2331.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective (stage 1), stereoselective (stage 3), intermediates after
each stage could be isolated, reactant assumed (chiral aminoalcohol),
metathesis reaction (stage 3), dropwise addition of Cbz-Cl (stage 1,
substage 1)
