$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 68-12-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a round bottom flask equipped with magnetic stir bar, L-tyrosine (200
mg, 1.2 mmol) was added and dissolved in DMF (8.0 mL, 0.15 M) followed by
the addition of EtN3 (157 mg, 1.56 mmol, 1.3 eq.) and DMAP (7.5 mg, 0.06
mmol, 0.05 eq.). The reaction flask was cooled in ice water for 15
minutes and CbzCl (224 mg, 1.32 mmol, 1.1 eq.) was added drop wise over 5
minutes. The reaction was monitored by TLC and until the starting
material was consumed over 5 hours. The mixture was diluted with EtOAc
(100 mL) and washed by HCl solution (1.0 M), saturated NaHCO3 (aq.),
brine and then dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. The solvent was removed under
reduced pressure to give the crude residue. Without column purification,
the crude Z-tyrosine was dissolved in DMF (8 mL, 0.15 M) and MeI (186 mg,
1.32 mmol, 1.1 eq.) was added. Next, oven dried K2CO3 (882 mg, 6.0 mmol,
5 eq.) was added to the reaction mixture was stirred for 10 hours, based
on TLC consumption of the starting material. The mixture was diluted with
EtOAc (100 mL), washed with HCl solution (1.0 M), saturated NaHCO3 (aq.),
brine and then dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. The solvent was removed under
reduced pressure to give the crude residue. Flash silica gel
chromatography (Ethyl Acetate/Hexane 40:60) was then applied to give the
protected amino alcohol. 285 mg (75% yield).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective (stages 1+2), intermediate Cbz-protected substrate from
stage 1 added in stage 2, dropwise addition of Cbz-Cl (stage 1, substage
1)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of substituted morpholines using stereodivergent aza-Michael
reactions catalyzed by Bronsted acids
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
